  <prompt>Replace the remaining 10 Placeholder verifiers in H13's acceptance-gate suite with real probes, one sub-task per verifier. This is the concrete work behind punch-list row B07 (H13 all-placeholders) — I1 already REAL (task 170 `PackagedScriptTenantLiteralInvariantVerifier`); `DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater` already REAL (task 184); this task delivers T1/T2/T3/T4/T5/T6 traps + I2/I3/I4/I5 invariants. Each sub-task follows the pattern established by `ArmSubscriptionReadinessProbe` (real probe) + task 170 (DI-swap in `E2EAcceptanceModule.cs`): (a) author real probe implementing `IE2ETrapVerifier` or `IE2EInvariantVerifier`; (b) swap in DI at `E2EAcceptanceModule` in place of `PlaceholderTrapVerifier` / `PlaceholderInvariantVerifier` for the SPECIFIC id; (c) unit tests (Pass / Fail / InfraFault outcomes); (d) commit per sub-task; (e) annotate punch list. HARD-BLOCKS task 186: without these 10 sub-tasks, `sprk_dataverseenvironment.SetupStatus` never reaches Ready and E2E fails.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in: task 170's real-probe + DI-swap ceremony pattern (`PackagedScriptTenantLiteralInvariantVerifier` reference); `IE2ETrapVerifier` + `IE2EInvariantVerifier` seam contracts; `E2EAcceptanceModule` verifier-registration surface; the 10 subject areas — KV `keyVaultReferenceIdentity` (T1), slot MI KV RBAC (T2), Graph app-role parity (T3), Exchange policy count (T4), slot MI KV RBAC role assignment (T5), SPE confidential-client (T6), Cosmos partition-key (I2), Dataverse App User pair (I3), SPE container ID tenant-derivation (I4), Graph per-tenant token scope (I5); DS-4 §6 H13 placeholder deep-dive rows; task 185 H13 aggregation wiring (this task feeds probes into that aggregator).</role>

  <goal>All 10 Placeholder verifiers replaced with real implementations, each swapped into `E2EAcceptanceModule` DI, each with Pass/Fail/InfraFault outcome tests, each committed atomically per sub-task, each annotated in `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B07 row's sub-task breakdown. `dotnet build` + `dotnet test` green. H13 aggregation gate (task 185) is now capable of returning Pass on a real customer stamp — task 186 can fire.

Per-sub-task deliverable (10 total):
- T1: `KeyVaultReferenceIdentityTrapProbe` (ARM.AppService read `Data.KeyVaultReferenceIdentity` on production + staging slots, compare to UAMI resource id)
- T2: real probe per DS-4 §6 T2 row
- T3: `GraphAppRoleParityProbe` (14 role assignments live via Graph REST)
- T4: `ExchangePolicyCountProbe` (sidecar read route per task 180 pipelining)
- T5: `SlotMIKvRbacRoleAssignmentProbe` (per DS-4 §6 T5 row)
- T6: `SpeConfidentialClientTrapProbe` (app-only token cert check per DS-4 §6 T6 row)
- I2: `AiSearchTenantFilterInvariantProbe` (unconditional tenantId eq filter enforcement per §4D I2 / FR-29)
- I3: `CosmosPartitionKeyInvariantProbe` (partition-key predicate enforcement per §4D I3 / FR-30)
- I4: `SpeContainerTenantDerivationInvariantProbe` (`ITenantContainerResolver` usage per §4D I4 / FR-31)
- I5: `GraphTokenTenantScopeInvariantProbe` (per-tenant token acquisition per §4D I5 / FR-32)</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 202's Class-B verification matrix row B07: "PARTIAL — 10 sub-tasks OPEN (task 204c scope)". I1 landed via task 170 (`PackagedScriptTenantLiteralInvariantVerifier`). `DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater` landed via task 184. The 10 remaining probes were sequenced as tasks 171/172/175/177/178/180 (T1-T6) + 173/174/176/179 (I2-I5) in TASK-INDEX.md pipelining visibility, but NONE of them landed (per Worker `Program.cs:847` comment + `PlaceholderInvariantVerifier.cs` retirement banner).

**Why this is task 186's HARD BLOCKER**: task 185 wired the H13 aggregation gate to sum 11 probes → 3 runners → Ready writer. Aggregation returns Pass only when all 11 probes return Pass. With 10 placeholders returning `InfraFault` unconditionally, aggregation NEVER passes, `SetupStatus` NEVER reaches Ready, and task 186 E2E fails at Wave G-7 acceptance. Task 186's dependency chain (185 → 184 → 113 → 162 → this task) is real.

**Sub-sub-phase escalation**: task 202 amendment notes "if any single T{N} or I{N} probe exceeds ~10h, sub-sub-phase 204c into 204c-{index}. Do NOT bundle 10 handlers into one megatask." The 40-80h range presumes ~4-8h per probe (I1's task 170 landed at ~6-9h per its own POML estimate); this task's executor SHOULD split into 204c-1 through 204c-10 individual POMLs if the first sub-task's real complexity exceeds ~8h. Splitting is a legitimate operator choice, not a task failure.

**Reference pattern**: `ArmSubscriptionReadinessProbe.cs` (H1 real probe landed by wave G — see punch list B06 `✅ APPLIED`) demonstrates the exact shape: probe class implements interface, unit tests cover Pass/Fail/InfraFault, DI registration in H1 handler's module. Task 170's `PackagedScriptTenantLiteralInvariantVerifier` + swap in `E2EAcceptanceModule.cs` is the H13-specific reference.</background>
