  <constraints>
    <constraint source="task-202 punch list verification obligation">Executor MUST grep-verify EACH sub-task's actual code state BEFORE applying — some of the pre-numbered tasks 171/172/173/174/175/176/177/178/179/180 may have partially landed via mid-batch work. If any sub-task's probe already exists, annotate `already-applied` + skip.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 BFF hygiene">N/A — L2 changes only, not BFF. But if any probe unexpectedly needs BFF code (e.g., calling a BFF endpoint for state check), STOP and escalate — probes should be READ-ONLY against Azure APIs, not against BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §8 test-modifying rigor override">Every sub-task adds/modifies `tests/**` — TEST-MODIFYING row triggers FULL rigor + `code-review` + `adr-check` at Step 9.5 UNCONDITIONALLY.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/testing.md">Probe tests MUST cover: Pass (real-world condition met) / Fail (real-world condition violated — the class-of-bug the probe exists to catch) / InfraFault (Azure API unreachable, retryable). No "always-Pass" fake tests — task 202's whole point is not accepting fake probes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §6 H13 placeholder deep-dive">Each probe performs INDEPENDENT re-verification, not trust of the handler's own reported success. That's the entire point of a terminal acceptance gate. Do NOT short-circuit by reading `RunStatus.HandlerReports[X].Outcome` — go re-read the underlying Azure/Cosmos/Graph/SPE surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§4D tenant-isolation invariants I2-I5">I2/I3/I4/I5 probes MUST ArchTest-scan the actual code call sites, not runtime traffic. I2 (AI Search tenantId eq filter), I3 (Cosmos partition-key predicate), I4 (`ITenantContainerResolver` usage for SPE), I5 (per-tenant Graph token acquisition). These are STATIC checks + LIVE checks combined.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 Component Justification">Each probe is a NEW class — but the seam (`IE2ETrapVerifier` / `IE2EInvariantVerifier`) already exists. §11 (1) Existing overlap: PlaceholderTrapVerifier/PlaceholderInvariantVerifier — this task REPLACES them; (2) Extension: not applicable — placeholder is a stub for the real probe; (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing: acceptance gate cannot go green → task 186 fails → project's stated FR-18/SC#5 (E2E provisioning demonstration) remains undemonstrated.</constraint>
  </constraints>

