  <escalation>
    <trigger name="sub-task-effort-exceeded" phase="Step 0.5">If task 171 T1 real-effort estimate exceeds ~8h (or any subsequent sub-task exceeds ~10h in-flight), SPLIT this task into 204c-1 through 204c-10 standalone POMLs. Do NOT force 10 probes into one megatask. Splitting is a legitimate operator choice per task 202 SESSION 7 amendment escalation-triggers section; this 204c POML then becomes an orchestration record referencing the 10 sub-POMLs. Task 186 dependency changes to `204c-1..204c-10 all complete` from `204c complete`.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any probe requires BFF code (calling a BFF endpoint for state check), STOP + escalate — probes should be READ-ONLY against Azure APIs (ARM / Cosmos / Graph / SPE), not against BFF. Redesign the probe.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any tenant-isolation invariant (I2/I3/I4/I5) probe surfaces a REAL production bug (unconditional tenantId filter missing, partition-key omitted, hard-coded container path, static-tenant Graph token), STOP + escalate per project CLAUDE.md § Human Escalation Triggers ("tenant-isolation invariant failure outside expected ArchTest work"). Fix path is per-invariant; do NOT let the probe silently return Pass on broken code.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any probe cannot be exercised against live Azure at author-time (subject handler not yet live-deployed), author against FAKES per DS-4 §6 "buildable earlier against fakes" note + flag LIVE-verification gap explicitly for task 186 Phase F rerun. Do NOT block this task indefinitely.</trigger>
